id: rust.dyn-vs-generic
kind: rust
title: dyn Trait vs generic bounds
aliases: dyn trait, static vs dynamic dispatch, boxed trait object
tags: api design, performance
questions:
  - when would you use dyn Trait instead of a generic parameter?
invariant: dyn gives one code path with runtime dispatch and heterogeneous collections; generics give per-type copies with compile-time dispatch.
answer_30s: Use dyn when the concrete type is chosen at runtime or implementations must be stored together; use generics when the type is known at compile time and the call is hot.
when_to_use:
  - runtime-selected implementations, heterogeneous collections, thin public APIs
avoid_when:
  - hot paths where the indirect call is measurable, or closed sets where an enum dispatch is simpler
related:
  - rust.traits
  - rust.generics-monomorphization
sources:
  - https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch18-02-trait-objects.html
